$ specir catalog build --help
Usage: specir catalog build [OPTIONS]

  Build a diagram catalog HTML bundle from a vistas registry or diagram store.

Options:
  --config PATH           Path to a legacy vistas.yml registry or a
                          hierarchical diagram store config.  [required]
  --out PATH              HTML file to write.  [required]
  --base-dir PATH         Base directory for template and vista source paths.
                          Defaults to the config file directory.
  --atoms-dir PATH        Directory with W5H1 atom markdown files to inject as
                          window.ATOMS_DB.
  --atoms-tag TEXT        Embed only atoms carrying this tag (full `ns:value`
                          or just `value`); repeatable. Default: all atoms.
  --strict-atoms          Fail the build if a spec `atoms:` id does not exist
                          among the loaded atoms (default: warning).
  --annotations           Save the page's annotations in an sldb store through
                          `sldb serve`; the server and the document can also
                          come from the page URL
                          (`?sldb=<url>&annotations=<id>`).
  --sldb-url TEXT         Base URL of `sldb serve --cors` that keeps the
                          annotations (implies --annotations).
  --annotations-doc TEXT  Id of the CatalogAnnotationsDoc that holds them
                          (implies --annotations). Default: derived from the
                          catalog's name.
  --help                  Show this message and exit.
rc=0

